CFG501 data legs (FROZEN_CRITERIA.md 7b71dd9b5): a copy of CFG498's cfg498_data.py with the draw taken from the UNSETTLED cold
energy.  Unsettled supply C_u = (1 - f_b) Int_0^{r_ta} (1 - m) dM_law (M_law = M_b nu, the law's total mass; m = the same clock profile
that tapers the phantom).  PRIMARY cap (scored): q_u = D / C_u; if q_u > 1 the tapered phantom is x 1/q_u.  Reported: CFG498's
full-supply cap (control C2) and the uncapped taper; KiDS with the two-halo frozen at CFG495's A = 0.07 against CFG413's best
x under the same frozen treatment.
--- CFG498 docstring follows ---
CFG498 data legs (FROZEN_CRITERIA.md d9c739010): the clock taper (no edge) with the capped, mass-conserving draw.
  object  phantom x m(r) out to r_ta (m from cfg487_lib.ShellClock: V1 rho_X = law mass, MS1 EXCEPTION; V2 rho_X = M_b(<r)/f_b,
          strict MS1); draw D = tapered phantom inside r_ta; available cold energy C = (1 - f_b) M_ta, M_ta = (4pi/3) r_ta^3
          (1 + delta_ta(z)) rho_m(z); q_raw = D / C.  PRIMARY cap: if q_raw > 1 the tapered phantom is x 1/q_raw.  REPORTED cap
          (outer-first): truncated where the tapered phantom reaches C.
